---
permalink: /feed.xml
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
site_url: "https://haraldrevery.com"
---
{#-
  RSS 2.0 feed for the Notebook, at /feed.xml.

  RSS 2.0 rather than Atom purely for reach: every reader understands it.
  <atom:link rel="self"> is the one Atom element RSS validators require.

  DATES: <pubDate> is RFC-822 (rfc822Date filter in eleventy.config.js), NOT the
  ISO format the sitemap uses. Readers dedupe on <guid>, so guid must stay the
  page's permanent clean URL — changing a post's slug creates a NEW entry in
  every subscriber's reader, which is why guid is the URL and not a hash.

  <lastBuildDate> is the newest POST date, never the build time: a feed whose
  channel date moves on every rebuild makes readers re-poll for nothing (same
  reasoning as <lastmod> in sitemap.njk).

  Description-only, no full text: posts from input_custom_html_pages/ are
  complete standalone documents copied verbatim (see the eleventy.before hook),
  so they have no templateContent to inline. A feed where half the entries carry
  full text and half carry none is worse than one that is consistently a teaser.

  DISCOVERY: eleventy_settings/base.njk emits the <link rel="alternate"> that
  points browsers and readers here.
-#}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom">
  <channel>
    <title>Harald Revery — Notebook</title>
    <link>{{ site_url }}/notebook</link>
    <description>Personal notes, essays and interactive experiments on music, mathematics, physics and photography.</description>
    <language>en-us</language>
    <copyright>Harald Revery</copyright>
    <lastBuildDate>{{ collections.notebook_posts | newestDate | rfc822Date }}</lastBuildDate>
    <atom:link href="{{ site_url }}/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" />
    <image>
      <url>{{ site_url }}/opengraphimg.jpg</url>
      <title>Harald Revery — Notebook</title>
      <link>{{ site_url }}/notebook</link>
    </image>
{%- for post in collections.notebook_posts %}
    <item>
      <title>{{ post.data.title }}</title>
      <link>{{ site_url }}{{ post.url | cleanUrl }}</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">{{ site_url }}{{ post.url | cleanUrl }}</guid>
      <pubDate>{{ post.date | rfc822Date }}</pubDate>
      {%- if post.data.description %}
      <description>{{ post.data.description }}</description>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- for tag in (post.data.tags or []) %}
      <category>{{ tag }}</category>
      {%- endfor %}
    </item>
{%- endfor %}
  </channel>
</rss>
